    "role": "system",
    "content": "你是正文作者。根据 manuscript_guide 的全文写法、chapter_assignment 的当前安排、materials 的来源内容，以及 accepted_body_markdown 中真实已写前文，继续完成同一篇文章。\n\n把本章要讲清的关系组织成连贯论述。由你决定章内解释顺序、段落组合、详略和小标题；写作安排不是逐项作答的模板。几项内容可以在同一比较或一组段落中一起讲清。材料中有帮助的机制、实验细节、条件和反例可以充分展开，重复的研究介绍则只保留当前讨论所需的部分。后章从前章已经建立的认识继续推进，不每次重启一篇小综述。\n\n以现象、机制、具体对象及其关系作句子主语，让相邻句接住同一个问题；来源编号只用于引用，不用内部 P 编号代替讨论对象。依据真实前文判断哪些解释已经完成；重返同一研究时只展开当前关系所需的新条件或比较。过渡直接承接问题与关系，避免反复用“上一章/本章/下一章将”介绍章节。标题服务于内容，不规定统一句式；段落讲清楚之后可以结束，无需每段补上重要性评价、局限声明或未来展望。不要把指南、工作安排、内部编号或给作者的指令写进正文。\n\n来源材料提供事实，指南提供写法。沿用给定引用身份；引用统一写成半角方括号 [P####]（例如 [P0001]），使用 materials 中确实存在的精确句柄，不写裸号、圆括号或自行编号；多个来源分别写成 [P0001][P0002]。保留数字和影响含义的条件，不编造来源，不把已有正文当作独立证据。处理相近或不一致表述时，用清楚的对象、范围和比较表达，不为行文顺畅虚构一致性。只在确实缺少必要材料时申请回读。\n\n本次交付 chapter_assignment 指定范围的新正文及其要求的表格或图示内容，不重发既有前文。没有固定段数、小节数、字数或引用数指标。不要输出思考过程或自评分。\n\n优先输出自然 Markdown 正文，最后附伴随记录：\n\n```guide_writer_metadata\n{\"complete\":true,\"remaining_content\":[]}\n```\n\n若确有尚未讲完的内容，complete 为 false，remaining_content 用简短自然语言说明具体缺口，不使用细纲任务 ID。例如“尚需比较两种方法在小样本情形下的差异”。不要为了填写字段虚构缺口，也不要用空泛的“需要更深入”代替缺口。\n\n也接受 JSON：{\"body_markdown\":\"本次正文\",\"complete\":true,\"remaining_content\":[]}。\n\n若需要尚未提供的材料，单独输出 {\"read_source_handles\":[\"来源句柄\"],\"read_atom_ids\":[]} 或用 read_atom_ids 指定已知原子，不能同时交付正文。现有材料已足够时直接成文。\n"
  },
  {
    "role": "user",
    "content": "{\n  \"manuscript_guide\": \"全文按\\\"临床关联证据—免疫机制—代谢物中介—外部干扰—主动干预—毒性管理—方法学与转化边界\\\"推进。引言与正文最终应实际引用至少150篇去重文献；引用必须参与论证，不为凑数机械平分到各章，也不把尚未写出的引言预先计入已完成指标。来源别名应统一处理：P0333与P0584、P0402与P0576、P0049与P0605等视为同一来源，避免重复计数；工具或检索导航标识不得充当正文文献编号。全篇反复出现的核心对象必须有明确主讲位置：Ch1负责观察性关联强度、队列异质性、方案修饰和证据阶梯入口；Ch2负责免疫机制链条并严格区分动物因果与人类关联；Ch3负责代谢物分子靶点、情境依赖和TME浓度缺口；Ch4负责抗生素、PPI、饮食和生活方式等外部暴露的时机、剂量、癌种背景与因果边界；Ch5负责FMT、定义菌群和活体生物药的临床转化、疗效异质性与证据等级；Ch6负责毒性预测、疗效/毒性耦合或解耦、供体与方案情境化安全管理；Ch7负责把前述瓶颈转为方法学设计原则。跨章承接要具体：Ch1让读者理解关联存在但不可普适，留下机制解释和干预验证问题；Ch2解释微生物如何进入先天和适应性免疫，但不解决代谢物浓度与外部扰动问题；Ch3把机制落到化学介质和受体通路，留下血浆与TME暴露脱节的问题；Ch4说明临床现实中的暴露如何重塑这些轴，留下主动干预是否可行；Ch5评估主动干预的疗效与边界，留下毒性管理问题；Ch6处理疗效与毒性如何耦合或解耦，留下预测和标准化难题；Ch7归纳为可执行研究设计。写作中不得使用同一种\\\"背景→机制→应用→局限\\\"模板套所有对象，也不得在每章结尾重复同一句证据不足。比较必须先明确维度：癌种、ICI方案、暴露时窗、基线/纵向、供体特征、宿主免疫状态、模型系统与人体证据、血浆/粪便与TME浓度。对可能性、条件性和阴性结果要保留原有限定：观察性关联不写成因果，动物模型不直接外推人类，血浆浓度不等同组织浓度，Phase II信号不写成Phase III确证，特定癌种或方案的结果不扩大为普适结论。关于P0593：该来源实际内容为别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌、增强肿瘤免疫原性的机制研究（小鼠CT26模型+人类膀胱癌回顾性队列），并非TACITO试验。正文中不得将P0593作为TACITO d-FMT联合ICI治疗mRCC的来源引用。P0593应在Ch3肌苷部分作为非微生物来源肌苷增效的平行机制证据使用，或在Ch5作为非菌群代谢干预的对比案例。mRCC中FMT联合ICI的随机证据应引用P0090系统综述中汇总的Phase II RCT数据（FMT联合pembrolizumab+axitinib，1年PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%）。\\n\\n全文章节写作安排：\\n\\nCh1 — 实体瘤中肠道微生物组与 ICI 疗效的临床关联证据\\n本章先建立\\\"有信号但无通用标志物\\\"的判断，再解释为何不能外推。顺序为：跨癌种阳性信号与反例 → 队列异质性与功能趋同 → 治疗方案修饰 → 外部药物暴露作为修饰变量 → 基线快照局限与纵向动态 → 证据阶梯表。跨队列统计、肠型、SCRUM-Japan、mCRPC反例和菌株级方案依赖共同支撑无普适标志物；JCOG2007在此主讲方案特异性，后章只回指。抗生素和PPI只保留总体效应量、关键时间窗和校正必要，详细剂量反应、HCC阴性、PPI机制留给Ch4。FMT-LUMINate、MIMic、MITRIC在表中只保留阶段、人群、主要结局和关键限制，机制与试验比较留给Ch5。本章结尾应留下两个问题：这些关联通过什么免疫机制表达，以及主动干预能否跨越观察性关联。\\n\\nCh2 — 微生物调节 ICI 疗效的免疫学机制\\n本章以机制链条组织，不按菌种罗列。顺序为：先天识别与DC启动 → 适应性启动与T细胞亚群 → 屏障、易位与髓系重编程 → 肿瘤类型和模型差异。每个节点都要区分证据层级：小鼠或体外因果、人类宏基因组或伴随观察、肿瘤内微生物边界。六酰化LPS、CD103+ DC、PD-L2/RGMb主讲先天和DC启动；分子模拟主讲适应性启动；P0098的Treg动态只作短回指，主要免疫中介留给Ch6。屏障部分要说明屏障损伤与疗效增强可以分离，细菌易位要区分主动免疫转运与被动漏肠，髓系部分要说明同一易位信号可产生促炎或抑制后果。最后用表格比较肿瘤类型机制与证据类型，不重复Ch1的临床关联强度。\\n\\nCh3 — 微生物代谢物的中介作用与分子机制\\n本章按分子靶点和情境条件组织代谢物，不按来源菌列表。先写SCFAs的双向性：PD-1背景下增强CD8+ T细胞和记忆，CTLA-4背景下可能促Treg或抑制DC共刺激；再写缺氧、葡萄糖剥夺和浓度阈值造成的效应反转。肌苷部分必须分开两条机制：肿瘤内在UBA6抑制与T细胞A2AR或碳源作用；临床只保留血浆关联和早期随机信号，并明确人体TME实测浓度缺失。胆汁酸与色氨酸代谢物围绕TGR5/FXR、AhR/RORγt等受体网络写局部与系统差异。功能通路部分由Ch2回指，但主讲放在本章，用于说明功能特征优于分类学。最后的TME浓度缺口要具体说明其阻碍剂量优化、因果推断和临床给药设计。P0593（别嘌醇/肌苷研究）在本章作为非微生物来源肌苷增效的平行证据使用：别嘌醇通过抑制XDH增加肌苷分泌→上调MHC-I和PD-L1→增强CD8+ T细胞杀伤，在CT26模型中联合抗PD-1实现4/6完全清除，人类膀胱癌回顾性队列（n=50）中抗痛风药使用者OS显著优于未使用者。此案例说明肌苷通路可被非菌群手段激活，但不能替代菌群来源肌苷的生理浓度讨论；其人类证据仅为小样本回顾性关联，不升级为因果。\\n\\nCh4 — 外部因素对微生物 - 免疫轴的干扰\\n本章主讲外部暴露如何改变微生物-免疫轴，并与Ch1的修饰变量概览分工：Ch1只给出效应量和时间窗入口，本章展开时机、剂量、药物类别、肿瘤背景和因果边界。抗生素按时间窗和疗程组织，加入HCC阴性结果与PD-L1分层，防止单一负面模型。PPI部分从流行病学关联转到口腔化易位、多样性下降和近期化疗修饰，并用H2B对照提出降级建议。饮食和生活方式部分区分食物基质、定义菌株补充剂和非标准化益生菌，避免把益生菌统一写成有益或有害。所有推断都要标注观察性证据和适应症偏倚，不能把药物暴露与疗效下降直接写成菌群因果链。\\n\\nCh5 — 微生物干预策略的临床转化现状\\n本章是主动干预的临床转化主轴。顺序为：初治人群信号 → 耐药人群边界 → 定义菌群和活体生物药 → 安全性边界 → 证据等级与标准化。FMT-LUMINate的疗效与\\\"有害菌丢失而非供体定植\\\"机制在此主讲；MIMic的定植动力学和生存数据也在此展开；MITRIC主讲阴性原因。Ch1的证据阶梯表只作为入口，本章不重复列表式介绍，而解释异质性来源。关于mRCC中FMT联合ICI的随机证据：细纲原将TACITO数据归于P0593，但P0593实际内容为别嘌醇/肌苷机制研究，不包含TACITO试验数据。本章mRCC FMT随机证据应引用P0090系统综述中汇总的Phase II RCT数据：FMT联合pembrolizumab+axitinib，1年PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%（p=0.036），ORR 54% vs 28%，未增加≥3级不良事件。此数据来自会议摘要级别的II期RCT，应标注证据等级为早期随机、小样本。不得在正文中引用不存在的TACITO具体数值（如12个月PFS 70% vs 41%、中位PFS 24.0 vs 9.0个月、P=0.053），除非后续获得独立来源确认。安全性部分与Ch6分工：本章保留干预安全边界和试验设计含义，毒性预测、耦合或解耦和管理策略留给Ch6。\\n\\nCh6 — 微生物组与免疫治疗毒性的关联\\n本章从毒性表型出发，不按药物列表。顺序为：结肠炎最强证据与因果验证 → 器官特异性和预测模型困境 → 疗效与毒性耦合或解耦 → 干预相关毒性的情境依赖 → 分子机制。Ch5已讲干预疗效与总体安全边界，本章新增的是毒性预测标志物、供体-方案交互和管理含义。FMT-LUMINate的Cluster B、Prevotella和Segatella copri数据在此主讲毒性情境，不再重述完整试验设计；P0284的屏障和代谢双重机制只保留与毒性相关的部分，详细机制回指Ch2。非结肠炎毒性必须明确样本量不足，不能把结肠炎结论外推到心肌炎或神经毒性。\\n\\nCh7 — 方法学挑战与未来研究方向\\n本章不是再次总结各章局限，而是把瓶颈转为可操作设计原则。顺序为：技术与标准化 → 观察性因果推断 → 临床证据与人群表征 → 未来方法。技术部分用标准化重分析和培养组学说明噪音与真实信号并存；因果部分强调反向因果、药物、饮食、年龄等混杂和孟德尔随机化边界；临床部分强调Phase III缺席、年龄、儿科、种族和TME浓度缺口；未来部分提出功能导向、多组学、AI、类器官或芯片和供体制剂标准化。引用应服务设计原则，不重复前文具体数值，也不把每个已知缺口写成全文唯一主线。\",\n  \"chapter_assignment\": {\n    \"chapter_id\": \"Ch2\",\n    \"title\": \"微生物调节 ICI 疗效的免疫学机制\",\n    \"writing_arrangement\": \"本章以机制链条组织，不按菌种罗列。顺序为：先天识别与DC启动 → 适应性启动与T细胞亚群 → 屏障、易位与髓系重编程 → 肿瘤类型和模型差异。每个节点都要区分证据层级：小鼠或体外因果、人类宏基因组或伴随观察、肿瘤内微生物边界。六酰化LPS、CD103+ DC、PD-L2/RGMb主讲先天和DC启动；分子模拟主讲适应性启动；P0098的Treg动态只作短回指，主要免疫中介留给Ch6。屏障部分要说明屏障损伤与疗效增强可以分离，细菌易位要区分主动免疫转运与被动漏肠，髓系部分要说明同一易位信号可产生促炎或抑制后果。最后用表格比较肿瘤类型机制与证据类型，不重复Ch1的临床关联强度。\",\n    \"required_content\": [\n      \"保留六酰化与五酰化LPS对TLR4/NF-κB和抗PD-1疗效的方向差异，并标注人类证据主要为宏基因组关联。\",\n      \"保留Ruminococcaceae菌株通过IRF8驱动CD103+ DC分化、迁移和CD8+ T细胞启动的证据及其动物模型边界。\",\n      \"保留PD-L2/RGMb轴作为微生物调节DC检查点语气的路径，并说明人体相对贡献未明。\",\n      \"保留P. bifermentans活菌屏障损伤与小分子组分增效的双重结构，避免把屏障损伤等同于疗效增强。\",\n      \"保留细菌易位可为DC/CCR7依赖的主动过程，以及MLN切除削弱远端抗肿瘤免疫的证据。\",\n      \"保留肿瘤类型机制比较表：肿瘤类型、关键微生物特征、主要机制或通路、证据类型、来源。\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"materials\": {\n    \"schema_version\": \"optomind.guided_body_materials.v1\",\n    \"evidence_atoms\": [\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e7d7af0a7b3edb140be223f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::53b453ed0d715e931ac64b6e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eb3e9143fc96593a3994a1b4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"1. 人类数据分析：整合7项临床研究、112例黑色素瘤患者的基线粪便宏基因组数据，进行批次校正后，比较响应者与非响应者之间的LPS生物合成基因（如lpxM, lpxL等）丰度差异，并进行功能肠型聚类分析。同时验证了肾细胞癌（RCC）小队列中的趋势。2. 体外实验：使用人源THP-1单核/巨噬细胞和小鼠RAW 264.7巨噬细胞系，检测六酰化和五酰化LPS对NF-kB激活和细胞因子分泌的影响，以及TLR4依赖性。3. 体内动物实验：在MC38皮下肿瘤小鼠模型中，使用粘菌素B（PMB，特异性结合LPS并耗竭革兰氏阴性菌）或广谱抗生素预处理，观察对抗PD-1疗效的影响；使用TLR4抑制剂TAK-242阻断信号；口服补充六酰化或五酰化LPS评估其对肿瘤生长和浸润T细胞的影响。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::30cfdfcac396e558c5bbf4cd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了基于LPS酰化状态（六酰化vs五酰化）的功能性微生物标志物，解释了为何单纯物种分类难以统一预测免疫治疗疗效。\",\n          \"limits\": \"主要临床数据来自黑色素瘤，仅在肾细胞癌小队列中观察到类似趋势，外推至其他实体瘤需谨慎。体内实验仅使用了单一小鼠肿瘤模型（MC38），未在其他模型中验证。宏基因组推断的LPS结构与实际粪便样本中测量的复杂混合物之间存在潜在差距，摘要未交代直接测量患者粪便LPS酰化状态的实验结果。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4574ed08573c4722aa904846\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"112例黑色素瘤患者基线宏基因组分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"响应者中编码六酰化LPS的基因（lpxM）显著富集，而非响应者中总LPS合成基因及编码五酰化LPS的基因（lpxL）更高。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cf8e3c7e4fcaea3829d02959\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"小鼠MC38肿瘤模型，抗PD-1治疗期间\",\n          \"finding\": \"使用粘菌素B（PMB）选择性耗竭产生六酰化LPS的细菌，或使用TLR4抑制剂TAK-242，均导致抗PD-1疗效丧失（肿瘤生长不受控）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6dfe07d80a5574e49e3c294a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"小鼠MC38肿瘤模型，口服补充LPS\",\n          \"finding\": \"口服六酰化LPS显著增强抗PD-1介导的抗肿瘤免疫（减少肿瘤负荷，增加肿瘤浸润IFNγ+/TNF+ CD8+ T细胞），而五酰化LPS无效且体外实验中可拮抗六酰化LPS诱导的免疫激活。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e9a88ce47aaabb6964b058ad\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::616574844e22d8b99e5cee57\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"既往研究指出产LPS细菌与较差预后相关，但不同细菌产生的LPS具有免疫刺激或抑制的双重性。本研究试图明确：肠道微生物群中不同结构LPS（特别是六酰化vs五酰化）是否比单纯的物种组成更能解释抗PD-1治疗的疗效差异？其具体的分子机制是什么？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ea04c7a3e4e96a4c62d81850\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究对象为接受抗PD-1免疫治疗的黑色素瘤患者（n=112，多队列合并）及小鼠模型（MC38结肠腺癌）。研究聚焦于肠道微生物群产生的脂多糖（LPS）结构差异对免疫治疗反应的影响，具体区分了六酰化与五酰化LPS的作用。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::26b75821d485346396d6f076\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究旨在解决肠道微生物群组成与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效之间关联不一致的问题，提出从物种分类转向功能代谢物结构的视角。作者通过分析112名黑色素瘤患者的基线粪便宏基因组数据，发现编码六酰化LPS的基因（lpxM）在临床响应者中富集，而总LPS合成基因在非响应者中更高。在小鼠模型中，通过抗生素选择性耗竭产生六酰化LPS的细菌或使用TLR4拮抗剂，证实了这种特定的LPS结构对于抗PD-1介导的抗肿瘤免疫是必需的；相反，口服补充六酰化LPS增强了抗PD-1疗效，而五酰化LPS无此效果甚至具有抑制作用。研究揭示了LPS酰化状态作为预测生物标志物和潜在治疗增强剂的潜力。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b09a7561428bbb9e03f39c73\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"论文指出既往研究将产LPS细菌与不良预后关联，但忽略了LPS结构的异质性。本文强调从物种水平转向功能/结构水平理解微生物-免疫互作的重要性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::60966113149da9091496cd88\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"使用宏基因组功能注释（KEGG orthologs）和批次校正（ComBat-Seq）来识别功能性肠型和基因丰度差异，而非仅依赖16S rRNA或物种分类。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ff5140480eb6af44c5698502\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限黑色素瘤患者数据为主，其他癌症类型证据不足。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物群通过产生特定结构LPS（六酰化）增强抗PD-1疗效的证据。显示响应者中lpxM基因富集，非响应者中lpxL（五酰化）基因富集。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::82c144196355ab11a203e772\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制主要在体外细胞系和小鼠模型中验证，人类体内的直接因果链条（如LPS浓度与免疫细胞活性的定量关系）尚需更多数据支持。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"阐明了六酰化LPS通过TLR4激活NF-kB和促进CD8+ T细胞浸润的具体机制。证明了TLR4信号对抗PD-1疗效的必要性（通过PMB耗竭或TAK-242抑制阻断疗效），以及六酰化LPS的促炎性与五酰化LPS的拮抗/抑制性对比。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2f016738f0638f6db35f7abc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的临床发现主要基于黑色素瘤，不能直接推广到所有实体瘤。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::db8d9cd6307630a080d5803a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"宏基因组数据推断的是基因潜力（lpxM/lpxL丰度），而非直接测量的LPS蛋白产物浓度，两者间的相关性在复杂粪便环境中未被完全量化。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::029508f7afa372167c3e7a82\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"小鼠模型中的TLR4信号机制可能与人存在差异（文中提及人鼠TLR4/MD2对LPS酰化状态的敏感性不同），需注意跨物种外推的风险。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::67b0201079430f7faeb6b427\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"粘菌素B（PMB）不仅耗竭特定菌群，还结合LPS，其效果是多因素的，解读时需区分是菌群改变还是LPS结合的直接效应（尽管文中倾向于前者，因为PMB保留了其他革兰氏阴性菌）。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1d8d3899c286dca10d450d80\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0080\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::856c2af998f7879e7615a726\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e932151205010d0bc98c4432\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::314c45c26bf753c80bb15dbe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::331eb326bdc2414f78041b69\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"As a review article, the approach involves a systematic narrative synthesis of published clinical and preclinical studies. The authors organize the material by therapeutic area (ICIs vs. Vaccines) and then by evidence type (Clinical Findings, Pre-Clinical Findings, Mechanisms, Manipulation Strategies). They compare and contrast findings across different cancer types and vaccine platforms to distill common themes, such as the roles of SCFAs, MAMPs, and cytokines. The review does not perform new primary research but aggregates and interprets existing data from cited references to build a conceptual framework for microbiome-immune-interaction.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2c442b509b02bfe68b4fd69b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive comparative framework linking microbiome modulation to two distinct but related immune interventions (ICIs and vaccines), identifying shared mechanistic pathways (SCFAs, MAMPs, cytokines).\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it does not provide quantitative meta-analysis or new experimental data. The synthesis relies on heterogeneous study designs, making direct comparisons difficult. Some mechanistic links are proposed based on correlative clinical data or single preclinical studies without full validation in human systems.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6893201ae8be196df66f979b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Highlights the potential clinical utility of microbiome profiling for predicting ICI and vaccine response, and outlines strategies like FMT, probiotics, and prebiotics for modulation.\",\n          \"limits\": \"The clinical evidence for microbiome manipulation (probiotics/prebiotics) is mixed and often lacks robust mechanistic correlation in humans. Many preclinical findings have not yet been translated into effective clinical therapies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d1b93d675e5ea37408a69ae6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Clinical studies in metastatic melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, and urothelial carcinoma treated with anti-PD-1/PD-L1 or anti-CTLA-4\",\n          \"finding\": \"Higher gut microbiome diversity and specific bacterial abundances (e.g., Faecalibacterium prausnitzii, Bifidobacterium longum, Akkermansia muciniphilia) are associated with improved ICI response and longer progression-free survival. Conversely, antibiotic use prior to or during ICI therapy is generally associated with reduced efficacy, although some studies show no association.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::401937b6bf1397ad67aa7641\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Preclinical mouse models (melanoma, colon cancer, renal cell carcinoma, fibrosarcoma)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Microbiota depletion via broad-spectrum antibiotics reduces ICI efficacy. FMT from ICI responders enhances anti-tumor immunity (increased CD8+ T cells, Th1 polarization) compared to FMT from non-responders. Specific bacteria (e.g., Bacteroides fragilis, Bifidobacterium pseudolongum) restore efficacy via mechanisms involving TLR signaling and metabolite production (inosine).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5a6ed862076f28bdb13cebb9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Clinical and preclinical studies of various vaccines (influenza, rotavirus, typhoid, etc.)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Germ-free and antibiotic-treated models consistently show reduced antibody responses to most vaccines, suggesting the microbiome is crucial for optimal vaccine efficacy. Specific microbial components like flagellin (via TLR5) and SCFAs (via GPR43) act as endogenous adjuvants or enhance exogenous adjuvant activity. Dysbiosis in infants and the elderly is linked to poorer vaccine responses.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4a9ad87a7c21e655b8d53364\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic investigations across both ICI and vaccine contexts\",\n          \"finding\": \"Three key factors mediate microbial immunomodulation: 1) Short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs) which can have context-dependent effects (promoting DC maturation in vaccines but potentially inhibiting it in ICI); 2) MAMPs (e.g., flagellin, peptidoglycan) which stimulate pattern recognition receptors (TLRs, NOD2) on APCs to prime immune responses; 3) Inflammatory cytokines (IL-12, IFN-gamma, IL-10) whose steady-state levels are shaped by the microbiome and influence systemic immunity.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cf4bc2b8106e28e4a47c272e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::94e93b0e9b694ea7de08b48e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review aims to address the heterogeneity in treatment success for immune-targeted interventions (ICIs and vaccines). It seeks to understand the role of the microbiome in determining these outcomes, identify key mechanisms of microbial immunomodulation, and explore how manipulating the microbiome could predict or improve therapeutic responses.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::022a5cdda6e257056e7a9edc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the interaction between the commensal microbiome and the host immune system, specifically examining how this interaction modulates the efficacy of two major classes of immune-targeted interventions: cancer immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) and vaccines. It covers clinical observations in human patients (primarily melanoma, non-small cell lung cancer, renal cell carcinoma, urothelial carcinoma for ICIs; various infectious disease vaccines for vaccination) and preclinical findings from mouse, pig, and chicken models.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a3d51880e6763980fb4e0fc2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This is a narrative review that synthesizes existing clinical and preclinical literature to elucidate the reciprocal interactions between the microbiome, the immune system, and the outcomes of immune interventions. The authors juxtapose studies from ICI therapy and vaccination to identify common microbial and immune elements. They discuss clinical associations between specific microbial signatures (e.g., Faecalibacterium prausnitzii, Akkermansia muciniphilia) and treatment response, as well as preclinical mechanistic insights involving microbial metabolites (short-chain fatty acids, inosine), microbe-associated molecular patterns (MAMPs), and inflammatory cytokines. The review also addresses the impact of antibiotics, probiotics, prebiotics, and fecal microbiota transplants (FMT) on intervention outcomes, highlighting the potential for microbiome-based strategies to improve therapeutic efficacy.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8677c0f361db12eb80393af3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"General introduction to how the microbiome educates the immune system, regulates homeostasis, and influences diverse immune processes including defense against infection and autoimmunity.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::52cd806f824b68dd3a0382db\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of how microbiome modulation affects vaccine outcomes, highlighting shared mechanisms (SCFAs, MAMPs, cytokines) and differences (e.g., live vs. inactivated vaccines).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::631f065d89bbef76014439c8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Review of clinical and preclinical efforts using FMT, probiotics, and prebiotics to improve ICI and vaccine outcomes.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::827da2bac4d68e9836b04872\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Associations are primarily observational in humans; causality is largely established in preclinical mouse models. Effects may vary by cancer type and ICI agent (anti-PD-1 vs anti-CTLA-4).\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific gut microbial signatures associated with ICI efficacy in solid tumors. Clinically, higher diversity and abundance of Faecalibacterium prausnitzii, Bifidobacterium longum, and Akkermansia muciniphilia are linked to better outcomes in melanoma, NSCLC, and RCC. Antibiotic use is frequently associated with reduced efficacy.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::38f1ad86e5e0d277737673b3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanistic details are derived from preclinical models (mice). The review notes that SCFA effects can be context-dependent (e.g., butyrate may inhibit ICI in some contexts while promoting vaccine response). Direct translation of these mechanisms to human tumor microenvironments requires caution.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details three main mechanistic pathways: 1) SCFAs (e.g., butyrate) influencing DC maturation and T cell activation; 2) MAMPs (e.g., flagellin, peptidoglycan) stimulating TLRs/NOD2 on APCs to promote Th1 polarization and antigen presentation; 3) Microbiome-derived cytokines (IL-12, IFN-gamma) shaping the immune tone.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7b5283260c0e718f8177c2a3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review covers multiple cancer types (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, urothelial) and ICI agents (anti-PD-1, anti-PD-L1, anti-CTLA-4). Findings should not be assumed to be uniform across all solid tumors or ICI types.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::31184bdeed7a8fc614b22a66\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic insights are from preclinical mouse models; direct applicability to human solid tumors requires verification.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::59e312711a840825fa208836\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Clinical associations are often correlative; causality is not always established in human studies.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::37411b100d5a12085cc1aa94\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide quantitative effect sizes or meta-analytic conclusions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f2e129e150923324a3e75d5a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0309\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::48cafa877ec53bf8522e21d0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4f61f40d6fb583a9f6aebd77\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8c8b08076ce7446e09ba8ac8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5a6cec745bdbbb96061f2d7a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用叙事性综述方法。作者通过梳理文献，从三个维度组织材料：(1) CRC免疫微环境的构成与空间分布；(2) 微生物组对免疫系统的作用机制（PRRs激活、代谢物调节、抗原呈递）与免疫系统对微生物组的反馈调节（IgA、细胞因子、PD-1）；(3) 微生物异质性与治疗反应性的关联，以及基于此的靶向干预策略（工程菌、代谢物补充、FMT、联合疗法）。文中引用了多项体外实验、动物模型研究及部分临床试验数据作为论据支持。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::210e5d2f07c93b43ec367efb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了CRC中微生物-免疫双向调控的系统性框架，整合了从分子机制（TLR4, AhR, IDO1）到临床表型（免疫沙漠vs炎症型）的多层次证据。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为综述，其结论依赖于所引用的原始研究，部分机制主要基于动物模型或回顾性分析，缺乏大规模前瞻性随机对照试验的直接证据来确立因果关系。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d9679d9a46d7d46637259e7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"明确了特定微生物标志物（如Fn/Fp比值）和治疗相关微生物（如产丁酸菌、B. fragilis）作为预测免疫治疗和化疗疗效的生物标记物的潜力。\",\n          \"limits\": \"关于微生物异质性的时空差异及其对个体化治疗的精确指导意义，目前仍停留在概念层面，缺乏标准化的检测流程和临床验证标准。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::06e3870d7f02968c8d88c04c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"总结了多种靶向干预策略（FMT、工程菌、代谢物补充），指出了当前转化的瓶颈（如供体匹配、载体安全性、伦理监管）。\",\n          \"limits\": \"大多数干预措施仍处于临床前阶段或早期临床试验阶段，长期安全性和有效性尚未得到广泛证实，且不同研究间的干预方案差异巨大，难以直接比较。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2cefaaf0e8ae5bbac1b597e1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"微生物通过TLR4/NLRP3通路及代谢物（NaB）\",\n          \"finding\": \"微生物可促进或抑制免疫反应。例如，TLR4激活可增强T细胞浸润或抑制肿瘤形成（取决于模型）；NaB通过抑制HDAC促进Treg增殖并抑制Th17分化，发挥抗炎作用。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fc4803ce7ded366b232efc6f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"特定微生物代谢物（如Fn来源的琥珀酸、B. fragilis多糖）\",\n          \"finding\": \"不同微生物对免疫治疗响应有差异化影响。Fn及其代谢物琥珀酸通过抑制cGAS-IFN-β通路导致抗PD-1耐药；而B. fragilis多糖可与CTLA-4抑制剂协同增强T细胞活化。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c74364048e9e293f7951aa75\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"IDO1/Kyn/AhR信号轴\",\n          \"finding\": \"微生物代谢物（如吲哚-3-羧酸）可通过调节IDO1-Kyn-AhR通路抑制Treg分化，增强CD8+ T细胞功能，从而提升抗PD-1疗效。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::89868760174da92467c74427\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"工程菌与纳米递送系统\",\n          \"finding\": \"工程益生菌（如表达IL-15/FLT3L或硒纳米颗粒的大肠杆菌Nissle 1917）可在动物模型中显著增强抗肿瘤免疫，但面临定植率低、生物安全性未明及缺乏临床验证等限制。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0e29441524f9c3b1e736fd7e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fef76e5a8d37b0e335a004f1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管已知微生物组-免疫轴在CRC进展中起关键作用，但具体的双向分子机制尚不完全清楚，且微生物异质性如何具体影响治疗结局（特别是免疫治疗耐药性）仍是未解之谜。本研究旨在综合现有证据，厘清这些机制并评估靶向干预的临床前景。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::af1641af42f83afb27a1845c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"结直肠癌（CRC）的免疫微环境，重点聚焦肠道微生物组与宿主免疫系统之间的双向调控机制。涵盖分子通路、代谢产物作用、免疫细胞互作及靶向干预策略。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3af66b0a8ed7e22ed6bc06ab\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇综述，旨在系统阐述结直肠癌中肠道微生物组与免疫系统的双向调节机制及其临床转化潜力。文章首先描述了CRC免疫微环境的组成特征，随后深入探讨了微生物通过模式识别受体（如TLR4、NLRP3）、代谢物（如短链脂肪酸SCFAs、次级胆汁酸）和抗原呈递影响免疫反应的分子机制；同时分析了免疫系统如何通过IgA、细胞因子（IL-17, IL-22）及PD-1通路反向调控微生物群落。此外，综述评估了微生物异质性对化疗和免疫检查点抑制剂疗效的影响，并讨论了工程菌、粪菌移植（FMT）及联合免疫治疗等靶向干预策略的现状与挑战。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5c7398e8e75cc3d1d39e0cd6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"文章第一部分关于CRC免疫微环境组成及空间分布的描述。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::43593b1651634ce8ff968fe9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"文章中关于不同CRC部位微生物组成和免疫浸润差异的讨论。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5dffc77189a6068a73be71cb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"文章中关于Engineered probiotics和Indole propionic acid nanoparticle delivery systems的章节。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cf74ca178c3b440b7a73380d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"主要基于CRC背景，其他实体瘤的数据较少；多为观察性关联或小样本研究，因果链条需结合其他实证研究确认。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了微生物组影响ICI疗效的具体临床关联和现象描述。指出高丰度的Fn与抗PD-1耐药相关，而B. fragilis和多糖类物质可增强免疫治疗响应。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b8e04f6cbd2d5473dc58d3c7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"许多机制细节来自小鼠模型（如MC38, AOM/DSS），在人体内的适用性存在不确定性；部分机制（如AhR）涉及复杂的转录调控，需结合其他研究验证其在人类患者中的普遍性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细阐述了介导微生物-IICI互作的分子机制。包括：1) Fn通过抑制cGAS-IFN-β通路减少CD8+ T细胞浸润；2) NaB通过HDAC抑制调节Treg/Th17平衡；3) IDO1-Kyn-AhR轴调节T细胞分化；4) 工程菌分泌细胞因子（IL-15, FLT3L）直接激活免疫细胞。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9269ca231cad202dabd3b46a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"大部分干预数据来自临床前研究或早期II期试验，缺乏III期确证性数据；供体选择和标准化问题尚未解决。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了基于微生物的干预策略（如抗生素清除Fn、FMT、工程菌）作为克服ICI耐药的潜在手段。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::03a9dd8d7e1e346260686ba8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述主要聚焦于结直肠癌（CRC），虽然提及黑色素瘤作为PD-1研究的参考，但其核心数据和机制推导均基于CRC。在推广到其他实体瘤时需格外谨慎。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6f04c00c6d39995005013387\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中提到的许多机制（如TLR4、NLRP3、AhR）在不同微生物和不同癌症类型中可能有不同的作用方向，不能简单地将CRC中的发现外推至所有情况。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5bba9c7c5d19a04f6e6645fd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"对于“工程菌”和“纳米递送”等干预措施，目前证据等级较低，主要为动物实验，不应将其视为已成熟的临床解决方案。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::57d746f0637f29f51cc5d18f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"微生物与免疫治疗的关联多为相关性研究，部分因果证据来自动物模型，需注意区分观察性关联与因果机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::db899adfd8eba3a3cb1242e2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0028\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e27d1d80c8c6c9f4ae73314b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b76674ea2e3d7482a5ef094c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2762f217d7608d2f8803516f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8ca1fa3ae7ea3b3b5329a4c6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"所给摘要未交代具体的实验设计细节（如动物模型类型、样本量、统计方法等）。根据摘要描述，研究路线包括：1. 从对PD-1治疗响应的实体瘤患者粪便中分离鉴定新型Ruminococcaceae菌株；2. 在动物模型中评估该菌株单独或与PD-1阻断联合使用的抗肿瘤效果，包括在非响应者粪便移植背景下的测试；3. 机制探究：分析该菌株对CD103+ DCs的刺激/成熟作用，检测IRF8驱动的DC分化、Toll样受体（TLRs）的激活以及DC在肿瘤和引流淋巴结中的积累；4. 分析DCs与CD8+ T细胞的互作，检测CD8+ T细胞的激活状态、PD-1表达水平、NFATc1核转位情况以及T细胞受体（TCR）库的多样性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fce30b3e668a1657ece1d813\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提出并验证了一种具体的分子和细胞机制：特定肠道细菌（Ruminococcaceae）通过IRF8依赖的途径激活CD103+ DCs，进而增强肿瘤特异性CD8+ T细胞的活化和PD-1表达，从而协同PD-1阻断疗法提高疗效。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代该发现的普适性范围（是否适用于所有实体瘤类型、不同患者亚群的效果差异）、菌株的具体分类学细节、动物模型与人类临床结果的直接对应关系、以及长期安全性数据。此外，虽然提到“非响应者”背景下的增效，但未明确说明这是否意味着完全逆转了耐药性或仅部分改善。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::70362be0850832eb8fdfe4e1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"在动物模型中，使用源自PD-1响应者粪便的新型Ruminococcaceae菌株，并与PD-1阻断联合应用（包括非响应者粪便移植背景）。\",\n          \"finding\": \"该菌株显著抑制了肿瘤生长。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c55de4c11d644214110ff8a6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"机制层面，该菌株作用于肠道免疫系统。\",\n          \"finding\": \"通过刺激多个Toll样受体，促进IRF8驱动的CD103+ DCs的分化、成熟及其向肿瘤微环境和肿瘤引流淋巴结的迁移与积累。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cf335aeca2ee1231aa9ee0b1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"在肿瘤微环境中，CD103+ DCs与CD8+ T细胞互作。\",\n          \"finding\": \"延长的互作导致多种肿瘤抗原特异性CD8+ T细胞的激活，并通过NFATc1核转位增强激活信号，促使这些细胞表达PD-1，形成富含PD-1+ CD8+ T细胞的效应细胞群，且具备更广泛的TCR库。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::943ec97204c69cc3b820ba83\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::37c687c4177ce6a85ea614eb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"核心问题是：肠道微生物群如何具体调节实体瘤中PD-1阻断治疗的疗效？特别是，是否存在特定的细菌菌株能够通过特定的免疫细胞通路来增强抗肿瘤免疫反应？动机在于解决当前对菌群-免疫疗法相互作用机制理解不足的问题，并探索潜在的生物标志物或辅助治疗手段。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5d8ce9d2761bd28fb3e893a6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究聚焦于实体瘤（solid tumors）中PD-1阻断治疗（PD-1 blockade）的疗效机制，具体研究对象为从对PD-1治疗有反应的实体瘤患者粪便中分离出的新型Ruminococcaceae科细菌菌株。研究情境涉及肠道微生物群与肿瘤微环境（TME）及引流淋巴结之间的免疫互作，主要关注该特定菌株如何影响树突状细胞（DCs）和CD8+ T细胞的激活过程。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::13e776749bbf274c6bc74295\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该论文旨在阐明肠道微生物群介导的免疫激活在PD-1阻断治疗临床疗效中的具体机制。尽管已知肠道菌群与免疫检查点阻断疗法的抗肿瘤疗效相关，但其详细机制尚不明确。作者通过动物模型实验发现，这种源自响应者粪便的新型Ruminococcaceae菌株能够有效刺激并成熟CD103+树突状细胞（DCs），促进其从肠道迁移至肿瘤微环境和肿瘤引流淋巴结。这些被激活的CD103+ DCs随后延长与抗原特异性CD8+ T细胞的接触，诱导多种肿瘤抗原特异性CD8+ T细胞的激活，并增强其PD-1表达。此外，该菌株还能通过NFATc1核转位增强T细胞激活信号。在动物模型中，将该菌株与PD-1阻断联合使用，甚至能显著抑制肿瘤生长，包括在非响应者患者的粪便移植背景下也显示出增效作用。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0c4947ec25af7ced35bbe9ec\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"从PD-1响应者粪便中分离出有效菌株，并在动物模型中验证其增效作用。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::391d1e32031245d4e1e2481b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"研究发现激活的CD8+ T细胞不仅表达PD-1，还具有更广泛的TCR库，表明PD-1+ T细胞在此语境下是有效的效应细胞而非耗竭细胞。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ba45edbbcb54a7c43bb26d91\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限于该特定菌株（Ruminococcaceae）和CD103+ DCs亚群。其他菌群或DC亚群可能通过不同机制起作用。动物模型结果不能直接等同于人体内的确切剂量和动力学。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道菌群增强PD-1疗效的具体细胞和分子机制：细菌通过TLRs刺激CD103+ DCs，经IRF8途径分化并迁移至TME和引流淋巴结，进而通过延长与CD8+ T细胞的接触并经由NFATc1信号通路增强其激活和PD-1表达。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::45419cbabdbf3d3db270910f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这是基于单一菌株的发现，不能代表所有有益菌的作用模式。非响应者背景下的效果需结合具体实验设计解读，可能存在个体异质性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"证实了特定肠道细菌（源自响应者）可以作为一种生物佐剂，增强PD-1阻断疗法在实体瘤中的临床疗效，即使在非响应者背景下也有潜在增效作用。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ac6072219974101c28b4c620\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究基于动物模型，其机制和疗效外推到人类患者时需考虑物种差异和临床环境的复杂性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::810821bd1ab41e4b7284737e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"仅涉及一种特定的Ruminococcaceae菌株，不能推广到整个肠道微生物组或其他细菌种类。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::67ca4d55509d27e18258a97b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"摘要未提供统计学显著性细节、样本量及重复次数，评估证据强度时需谨慎。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9cd4b7884f4f52223ba2f677\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"“非响应者”背景下的实验结果可能受供体粪便复杂成分的影响，需区分是菌株本身的作用还是菌群整体重塑的结果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4c6df7ed32c2126fd9ae9a6c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::cc99c3d791586bf600998617\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::714fa5fb3739da3cf616b8e9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::27f0c1ae70df13232e67b082\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::558d9a1781a6ec4ec879b80a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"1. **动物模型构建**：使用无菌鼠（GF）、抗生素处理鼠（ABX）以及定植健康人/小鼠微生物群（HMB/MMB）或患者粪便的C57BL/6小鼠，植入多种肿瘤细胞系（MC38, B16-OVA等）。 2. **免疫表型分析**：利用流式细胞术分析肿瘤、引流淋巴结（dLNs）和肠系膜淋巴结（MLNs）中免疫细胞亚群（CD8+ T, CD4+ T, DCs等）的频率、活化标志物（Granzyme B, IFNγ, TNFα）及检查点分子（PD-L1, PD-L2, RGMb）的表达水平。 3. **干预实验**：给予抗PD-L1、抗PD-1、抗PD-L2抗体（区分结合PD-1或RGMb的特异性克隆）或抗RGMb抗体单药或联合治疗，评估肿瘤生长和生存率。 4. **机制验证**： - **细菌筛选**：通过单一抗生素筛选和16S rRNA测序，从HMB中分离出能增强抗肿瘤反应的特定菌株（如C. cateniformis），并进行单菌定植实验。 - **体外共培养**：将细菌提取物处理骨髓来源树突状细胞（BMDCs），再与OT-I CD8+ T细胞共培养，检测T细胞活化。 - **基因编辑**：构建RGMb条件性敲除小鼠（T细胞特异性或巨噬细胞特异性），验证RGMb在不同细胞类型中的作用；使用过表达PD-L2的BMDCs进行回输实验，确认PD-L2下调是细菌发挥作用的必要条件。 5. **临床相关性验证**：将来自黑色素瘤完全响应者（CR）和无响应者（NR）患者的粪便移植到无菌鼠中，模拟临床耐药情境，测试联合疗法的疗效。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::08b13b4b157e8ef1ff4f4899\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了肠道微生物群通过下调DCs上的PD-L2表达来促进抗肿瘤免疫的新机制。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代该机制在其他肿瘤类型或人类患者中的普遍性验证数据。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::20fb710b0a0af4aac14e1fe1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"明确了PD-L2/RGMb轴是微生物依赖性耐药的关键靶点，并证明了联合阻断该轴可克服GF/ABX模型及部分患者来源模型的耐药。\",\n          \"limits\": \"主要基于小鼠模型，虽然使用了患者粪便移植，但尚未提供直接的人体临床试验结果，转化潜力尚待验证。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a34d3e822652fbf8fcd38aa5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"鉴定了具体细菌物种（C. cateniformis）及其作用机制（通过表面提取物下调PD-L2），为益生菌疗法提供了候选菌株。\",\n          \"limits\": \"仅鉴定了少数几种细菌，且指出并非所有促炎细菌都通过此机制起作用（如E. ramosum不显著抑制PD-L2），其他机制可能并存。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a86940ae13399bd89ace0f97\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"阐明了RGMb在T细胞上的新型抑制性功能，此前研究多关注其在髓系细胞或神经系统的作用。\",\n          \"limits\": \"RGMb在人体T细胞中的表达模式及功能是否与小鼠完全一致，材料中未提供直接证据。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1c86cb9f75c28b1d4e2c2bd4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"ABX/HMB vs ABX小鼠，MC38肿瘤模型\",\n          \"finding\": \"定植健康人微生物群显著增强了抗PD-L1治疗的效果，表现为肿瘤内CD8+ T细胞比例增加、耗竭标志物减少及效应功能增强；同时，在引流淋巴结中， responder小鼠的DCs上PD-L2表达显著降低，而PD-L1升高。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::02fe730e65f5325fef85f568\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"GF或ABX小鼠，MC38/B16等肿瘤模型\",\n          \"finding\": \"单独使用抗PD-L1或抗PD-1无法抑制这些模型中的肿瘤生长；但联合使用抗PD-L2（阻断RGMb相互作用）或抗RGMb抗体可显著抑制肿瘤生长，证明PD-L2/RGMb通路介导了微生物依赖性的耐药。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5095fd431387ffd441d38baf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"GF小鼠定植患者粪便（CR vs NR）\",\n          \"finding\": \"定植无响应者（NR）粪便的小鼠对PD-L1单药治疗无反应，但联合抗PD-L2治疗后肿瘤显著缩小且生存期延长，表明该策略可克服由患者自身微生物群导致的耐药。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::45c1d3a0900b76a03cf3aef7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"单菌定植实验\",\n          \"finding\": \"从HMB中鉴定的革兰氏阳性厌氧菌Coprobacillus cateniformis单菌定植即可重现HMB的抗肿瘤效果，并显著下调DCs上的PD-L2表达；其表面提取物在体外也能通过MYD88依赖途径抑制PD-L2表达。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b72644777a4fd00f9afde2f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"RGMb条件性敲除小鼠\",\n          \"finding\": \"仅在T细胞中敲除RGMb即可改善抗PD-L1治疗的抗肿瘤效果，而在巨噬细胞/粒细胞中敲除则无效，表明RGMb在T细胞上的抑制性信号是关键机制。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::687760ef661c1b7291e43c84\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c86ac1ffe4bd21a78303faa2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"肠道微生物群促进抗肿瘤免疫的具体分子机制是什么？为何部分患者对PD-1/PD-L1治疗无响应？如何通过靶向微生物相关的免疫检查点通路来克服这种耐药性？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::18a34261580a8ccbe9b80ac9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"小鼠肿瘤模型（MC38结肠癌、B16黑色素瘤等），涉及无菌鼠（GF）、抗生素处理鼠（ABX）及定植人类/小鼠微生物群的模型；研究对象为肠道微生物群、免疫检查点分子（PD-L2, RGMb）及T细胞功能。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::02ad5e4a95efd520cc9bf3a4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在揭示肠道微生物群如何调节抗肿瘤免疫反应，特别是针对PD-1/PD-L1抑制剂治疗无响应的情况。研究通过对比不同微生物状态下的免疫反应，发现微生物群通过下调树突状细胞（DCs）上的PD-L2表达来促进抗肿瘤免疫。进一步研究发现，PD-L2不仅结合PD-1，还结合排斥性导向分子b（RGMb）。在缺乏有益菌的模型中，PD-L2和RGMb的高表达抑制了CD8+ T细胞的活性。通过联合阻断PD-L2/RGMb通路或特异性敲除T细胞中的RGMb，可以克服由微生物缺失引起的对PD-1/PD-L1治疗的耐药性。研究还鉴定出特定细菌物种（如Coprobacillus cateniformis）能够诱导这种PD-L2下调，并验证了该机制在人源粪便移植模型中的潜在转化价值。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d7810546906ab0c15cc83ddc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"论文指出FMT疗效可变，且益生菌并未显示出类似生存获益，甚至可能有负面影响，突显了理解具体机制的重要性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3e3944d04adbbe12dd0b61fc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"论文提到其他细菌可通过分泌肌苷、muropeptides或STING激动剂发挥作用，而本研究聚焦于PD-L2/RGMb轴。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::edbb9bfef88fcc7792e0d24a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"论文展示了在定植非响应者患者粪便的小鼠模型中，联合疗法的有效性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a0695a1653ccfa8f2a8a4475\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"该机制主要在mouse models中验证；需注意的是，PD-L2也结合PD-1，作者通过抗体克隆特异性排除了PD-1结合的主要贡献，强调了RGMb的作用，但在人体中PD-L2/PD-1与PD-L2/RGMb的比例关系尚不明确。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细阐述了微生物群通过下调DCs表面PD-L2表达来增强抗肿瘤免疫的机制；并进一步发现PD-L2通过与T细胞表面的RGMb结合发挥抑制作用，而微生物的存在降低了这一抑制性互作。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c1da304bfc43c2d641ded0b0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"效果依赖于特定的肿瘤模型和微生物背景；并非所有肿瘤类型（如E0771乳腺癌）均显示联合治疗的额外获益，提示该策略具有肿瘤类型特异性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了克服微生物依赖性ICI耐药的策略证据：联合使用抗PD-L2或抗RGMb抗体可恢复对PD-1/PD-L1治疗的敏感性，即使在定植了非响应者粪便的模型中也有效。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::18cc47a4e9db7ec92c95e9bc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅从复杂菌群中筛选出少数几种，且指出其他菌群可能通过不同机制（如分泌肌苷、STING激动剂等）发挥作用，因此不能代表所有微生物效应。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"识别了促进ICI疗效的具体细菌物种（C. cateniformis），并证明其通过表面提取物抑制PD-L2表达，建立了特定菌群-宿主免疫分子-治疗反应的因果链。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b374f443c51adcef03a06d33\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的结论主要基于小鼠模型，尽管使用了患者粪便移植，但不能直接外推至人体内的确切疗效和安全性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::63cfbef8b6cb644b598a7d39\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"PD-L2/RGMb轴的作用是在特定微生物背景下（如GF或ABX）被凸显的，在正常SPF小鼠中，由于PD-L1已能有效抑制肿瘤，联合PD-L2阻断的额外获益有限或不显著，需注意适用情境。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::95630d39569adbe802ef0f43\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作者声称RGMb在T细胞上的作用是“novel”，但这基于其之前的研究焦点主要在髓系细胞，综述中应客观表述为“补充了RGMb在T细胞功能方面的新见解”。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::338a2c35c06fa7290f6f25f9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-8c71e871c7aa5482d545\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-f85da31c482f020fe5f7\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a7a6e9bd3a48b1fef12e\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-12c6cac6a4bef2539d08\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-02faf8b9fedd6313c05e\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-970b424322e405f5652d\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-f4e5574773433f48fdb6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-2fbf9fdf4b39e967b994\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-f9da8f3ea073b672e0db\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5c16b29821e421056954\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-f789746790cfca26b36b\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5c7f4595c3f7f0bfe107\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::50f6b2c5ac9bd691e19ea9f5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::113e9e24698e48b617801ee8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::13d62ece3687ca3ff02b6c26\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ccd742ea527af43296074069\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究设计为前瞻性、多中心、单臂II期临床试验。入组标准包括：NSCLC患者需PD-L1 TPS ≥50%且无一线可操作基因改变；黑色素瘤患者不限BRAF状态。所有患者在开始ICI治疗前一周内接受来自健康供体的单次FMT（口服胶囊）。主要终点是NSCLC队列的ORR。次要终点包括黑色素瘤ORR、1年无进展生存期（PFS）、总生存期（OS）、疾病控制率（DCR）及安全性。微生物组分析采用鸟枪法宏基因组测序，结合定量PCR和高通量培养组学验证细菌变化。此外，通过血浆代谢组学和流式细胞术分析免疫代谢景观，并在抗生素处理的荷瘤小鼠模型中通过回输“丢失”的细菌混合物来验证因果机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1876e77f5afb8193a6a5257e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的临床活性证据，证实FMT可提高ORR。识别出“基线有害菌清除”作为潜在的药效学生物标志物，并揭示了其与色氨酸代谢抑制及CD8+ T细胞扩增的关联。\",\n          \"limits\": \"研究为单臂设计，缺乏安慰剂对照，难以完全排除自然病程或其他混杂因素。样本量较小（每队列20人），限制了亚组分析和统计效力。黑色素瘤队列中观察到的严重毒性信号（如心肌炎）需要更大规模的随机试验进一步确认。供体选择对毒性的影响提示个体化差异，但具体筛选标准尚未确立。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::999c7dbb4eb04f853f51ce68\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"NSCLC患者接受FMT+抗PD-1\",\n          \"finding\": \"ORR达到80%（16/20），满足主要终点；1年OS为100%；未观察到3级及以上与治疗相关的不良事件。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ef45091c05d3c80087467567\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"黑色素瘤患者接受FMT+抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4\",\n          \"finding\": \"ORR为75%（15/20）；观察到较文献报道更早发生的严重免疫相关不良反应（irAEs），包括心肌炎；部分严重AEs与富含Prevotella的供体有关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0c4539dfe7511b5ee26afddc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"微生物组分析与临床响应关联\",\n          \"finding\": \"响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）相比，在FMT后表现出显著更高的基线细菌物种丢失幅度。这种丢失主要由有害菌（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus）构成，而非供体菌株的定植。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f77d7a57b1c5af196e7ec273\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"机制验证（动物实验）\",\n          \"finding\": \"在抗生素处理的小鼠中，将FMT响应者基线样本中丢失的有害细菌混合物重新引入，抵消了FMT联合ICI的抗肿瘤效应，证实消除有害菌是治疗获益的必要条件。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c5bc8bb178fbe4aff2844625\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::48e81723cf1694edffb2648d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管免疫检查点抑制剂改善了NSCLC和黑色素瘤的预后，但超过半数的患者存在原发性耐药。目前尚不清楚健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1（NSCLC）或抗PD-1联合抗CTLA-4（黑色素瘤）在一线治疗中的临床活性和安全性，以及FMT增强ICI疗效的人类机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f10ae71e3af0e5426782b275\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究针对晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和皮肤黑色素瘤患者，评估健康供体粪便微生物群移植（FMT）联合一线免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的临床疗效、安全性及机制。NSCLC队列接受抗PD-1单药治疗，黑色素瘤队列接受抗PD-1联合抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制治疗。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bfc280fdf99afe8f46ce98b5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"这是一项多中心、开放标签的II期临床试验（FMT-LUMINate），旨在评估单次口服胶囊FMT在启动ICI治疗前对原发性耐药患者的影响。研究纳入20名NSCLC患者和20名黑色素瘤患者。主要终点为NSCLC队列的客观缓解率（ORR）。结果显示，NSCLC队列ORR为80%，超过预设阈值；黑色素瘤队列ORR为75%。安全性方面，NSCLC组无3级及以上不良事件，而黑色素瘤组出现较早发的严重免疫相关不良反应（irAEs），特别是心肌炎，且与特定供体菌群有关。机制研究发现，响应者并非通过获得特定的供体菌株定植获益，而是通过显著清除基线存在的有害细菌物种（如Enterocloster和Clostridium属），从而降低色氨酸代谢途径活性并改善全身免疫微环境。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ada46cc65142f66137be5912\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅适用于未经过ICI治疗的原发性耐药患者；NSCLC结果基于高PD-L1表达人群；黑色素瘤结果包含不同BRAF状态。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT联合ICI在NSCLC（抗PD-1）和黑色素瘤（抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中的具体ORR数据（分别为80%和75%），证明了其在一线治疗中提高临床活性的能力。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1440b6c81c7ea354a5c0604d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制主要在人类队列中通过相关性分析发现，并通过小鼠模型进行功能验证；不同肿瘤类型中富集的有益菌种类有限重叠，但有害菌清除模式一致。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"阐明了FMT起效的潜在机制：响应者的获益主要依赖于基线有害细菌物种（如Enterocloster, Clostridium）的大量丢失，而非供体菌株的成功定植。这种丢失与血浆中色氨酸代谢产物（喹啉酸、犬尿氨酸）水平的降低以及效应性CD8+ T细胞的增加相关。动物实验证实，重新引入这些丢失的有害菌会阻断ICI疗效。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d56ff3d1c73603487584373\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅在黑色素瘤双免疫治疗队列中观察到显著的毒性信号；在NSCLC单药治疗或未使用双免疫治疗的既往研究中未观察到相同程度的毒性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了特定供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制（抗PD-1/CTLA-4）背景下严重免疫相关不良反应（如心肌炎、早期发作的3级以上AEs）之间的关联。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2631f5b2da9f5640b19f7f49\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"研究指出FMT疗效不依赖于供体-宿主相似性或菌株水平定植，而是依赖于基线微生物组的整体重塑和有害菌清除。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5a5656eba7a625dd6b12644d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"提到TACITO试验也观察到类似的结果，即在FMT组中观察到基线物种的消除，而在安慰剂组中没有。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f453542c412b162f0e6a8104\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的机制结论（有害菌清除导致疗效）是基于观察性关联和小鼠功能验证，需谨慎推断其在所有FMT场景下的普适性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f5dfc4aabe5eadd2a5f8c90b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"黑色素瘤队列中的严重毒性信号可能与双免疫检查点抑制的背景有关，不能直接外推至单药ICI治疗。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b12e17c00b7f89529c4a3847\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"供体选择对毒性的影响提示个体化差异，但本研究未建立标准化的供体筛选算法，仅作为警示。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::78071e0f85770a550546484c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"NSCLC队列的高ORR可能受限于高PD-L1表达人群的预后较好，需注意人群特异性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0223323bb5c9771bfce68f11\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"current_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\",\n            \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::456d19e731aeafe092b5f494\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"paper_title\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6edcdf66c26215bc9744d2b6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"plain_text\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6daa66dcd75ef6a88df089e5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"prior_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究人群：NSCLC队列（n=20，一线治疗，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，无既往抗PD-1暴露）；黑色素瘤队列（n=20，一线治疗，允许既往辅助抗PD-1但需停药>6个月）。干预措施：单次健康供体粪便微生物移植（FMT，口服胶囊）后紧接着启动ICI治疗。NSCLC组使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）单药；黑色素瘤组使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4（双ICI）治疗的ORR为75%（15/20）。关于毒性信号，在黑色素瘤双ICI组中观察到严重不良事件（AEs）的发生率较高且起病更早：13名患者（65%）经历了3级或更高级别的AEs，其中腹泻或结肠炎是最常见的3级及以上AE（20%的患者），另有15%的患者出现心肌炎。严重毒性的中位起病时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后40天，早于文献报道的60天。相比之下，NSCLC单药抗PD-1组无3级或以上AEs发生。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和黑色素瘤中的具体客观缓解率（ORR），以及双免疫检查点抑制剂（dual ICI）治疗下的毒性信号特征。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"该研究通过FMT-LUMINate II期临床试验评估了FMT联合ICI在两种不同癌症背景下的临床活性与安全性。结果显示，FMT显著提高了NSCLC患者对单药抗PD-1治疗的反应率（80%），并改善了黑色素瘤患者对双免疫检查点阻断（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4）的反应率（75%）。然而，在黑色素瘤双ICI背景下，FMT联合治疗伴随着更高的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）风险，特别是心肌炎和早期发作的严重毒性。这种毒性信号与特定供体来源的微生物群（富含Prevotella spp.）有关，且仅在双ICI背景下出现，而在单药抗PD-1背景下未观察到类似毒性。这表明FMT的安全性与特定的ICI治疗方案及供体微生物特征存在交互作用。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": []\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::497b875e9b14be91a0c84f61\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"prior_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\",\n              \"finding\": \"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R23\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\",\n            \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\",\n            \"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e34ebbbb34ba3c89d1c553df\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究人群：NSCLC队列（n=20，一线治疗，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，无既往抗PD-1暴露）；黑色素瘤队列（n=20，一线治疗，允许既往辅助抗PD-1但需停药>6个月）。干预措施：单次健康供体粪便微生物移植（FMT，口服胶囊）后紧接着启动ICI治疗。NSCLC组使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）单药；黑色素瘤组使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4（双ICI）治疗的ORR为75%（15/20）。关于毒性信号，在黑色素瘤双ICI组中观察到严重不良事件（AEs）的发生率较高且起病更早：13名患者（65%）经历了3级或更高级别的AEs，其中腹泻或结肠炎是最常见的3级及以上AE（20%的患者），另有15%的患者出现心肌炎。严重毒性的中位起病时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后40天，早于文献报道的60天。相比之下，NSCLC单药抗PD-1组无3级或以上AEs发生。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和黑色素瘤中的具体客观缓解率（ORR），以及双免疫检查点抑制剂（dual ICI）治疗下的毒性信号特征。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"该研究通过FMT-LUMINate II期临床试验评估了FMT联合ICI在两种不同癌症背景下的临床活性与安全性。结果显示，FMT显著提高了NSCLC患者对单药抗PD-1治疗的反应率（80%），并改善了黑色素瘤患者对双免疫检查点阻断（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4）的反应率（75%）。然而，在黑色素瘤双ICI背景下，FMT联合治疗伴随着更高的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）风险，特别是心肌炎和早期发作的严重毒性。这种毒性信号与特定供体来源的微生物群（富含Prevotella spp.）有关，且仅在双ICI背景下出现，而在单药抗PD-1背景下未观察到类似毒性。这表明FMT的安全性与特定的ICI治疗方案及供体微生物特征存在交互作用。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": []\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::436fcf7aa325545c7b4b35ba\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\",\n              \"finding\": \"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R23\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\",\n            \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\",\n            \"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1e65c84abaf39bc948ae4e34\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\",\n            \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b581c9a20631821c53f134ac\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"questions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"gap_key\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n          \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"required_output_ids\": [\n            \"O01\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bdf06d41fae85cb4002eea7d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The authors explicitly state that this is a phase 2 trial, not a phase 3 trial. They mention that the findings will be assessed as part of the CanBiome2 randomized trial (NCT06623461), which is described as a randomized trial evaluating FMT in combination with ICI in 128 patients, but the current paper does not report the results of this phase 3 trial. The study design was open-label and single-arm for the cohorts reported here, lacking the randomization required for a phase 3 RCT status.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires evidence of a completed large randomised phase III trial. This material provides only a phase 2 trial. While the authors reference an ongoing/forthcoming phase 3 trial (CanBiome2), they do not provide its results or confirm its completion within this text.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of FMT-LUMINate, a multicenter, open-label, phase 2 trial evaluating healthy donor fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) combined with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) or melanoma. The trial enrolled 40 patients (20 NSCLC, 20 melanoma). In the NSCLC cohort receiving anti-PD-1 monotherapy, the objective response rate (ORR) was 80%. In the melanoma cohort receiving dual anti-PD-1 and anti-CTLA-4 therapy, the ORR was 75%. The study found that clinical response was associated with the loss of baseline deleterious bacterial species rather than the engraftment of donor-specific strains. Safety data indicated no grade 3+ adverse events in the NSCLC cohort, but a higher incidence of severe immune-related adverse events (including myocarditis) in the melanoma cohort, particularly among recipients of donors rich in Prevotella spp.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e56bf9725ffb96585d3b26d8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The authors explicitly state that this is a phase 2 trial, not a phase 3 trial. They mention that the findings will be assessed as part of the CanBiome2 randomized trial (NCT06623461), which is described as a randomized trial evaluating FMT in combination with ICI in 128 patients, but the current paper does not report the results of this phase 3 trial. The study design was open-label and single-arm for the cohorts reported here, lacking the randomization required for a phase 3 RCT status.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires evidence of a completed large randomised phase III trial. This material provides only a phase 2 trial. While the authors reference an ongoing/forthcoming phase 3 trial (CanBiome2), they do not provide its results or confirm its completion within this text.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of FMT-LUMINate, a multicenter, open-label, phase 2 trial evaluating healthy donor fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) combined with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) or melanoma. The trial enrolled 40 patients (20 NSCLC, 20 melanoma). In the NSCLC cohort receiving anti-PD-1 monotherapy, the objective response rate (ORR) was 80%. In the melanoma cohort receiving dual anti-PD-1 and anti-CTLA-4 therapy, the ORR was 75%. The study found that clinical response was associated with the loss of baseline deleterious bacterial species rather than the engraftment of donor-specific strains. Safety data indicated no grade 3+ adverse events in the NSCLC cohort, but a higher incidence of severe immune-related adverse events (including myocarditis) in the melanoma cohort, particularly among recipients of donors rich in Prevotella spp.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ffe022f4ac7a2eb8241e5388\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a91f0ed643887e9f1b1d\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ef95a97dcd7bd8c151c4\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-501f35983c2f020a5c71\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-81ec1ef0c2a046851171\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-d46f32b2af56fa1c47e2\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-02757a568956f4b210b5\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-47775c7896730e2260bc\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b08d87be9985923039c9\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-4d651eaa044aee02c8ec\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-1294ef6fcf50c0be4a42\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-6e217865835c2f670e17\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b1f79ce65e003459f3ed\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-786845b1cd45dd24fdc8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-f0ebbdf389d42cf46d30\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::11e07541ccca87380640aaae\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"tool_supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的客观缓解率（ORR）具体数据，以及安全性特征。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在FMT-LUMINate试验中，接受健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1单药治疗的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者（n=20），其客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者（n=20），ORR为75%（15/20）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"NSCLC队列：一线治疗，无驱动基因突变，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）。黑色素瘤队列：一线或既往辅助治疗后复发>6个月，使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"揭示供体菌群特征（Prevotella富集）与特定毒性（心肌炎、3级及以上AEs）的关联机制，强调治疗背景（双免疫抑制 vs 单药）的关键调节作用。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"供体微生物组聚类显示，Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.，如Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）FMT的患者发生了严重的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），包括3例心肌炎（发生率15%），且发病时间显著提前（中位40天，而文献报道通常为60天）。其中2例心肌炎患者均接受了供体5的FMT，发病迅速（分别为第22天和第25天）。统计分析显示，Cluster B供体的粪便仅在双PD-1和CTLA-4阻断背景下导致毒性（P=0.051），而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下未观察到此类毒性。此外，S. copri的定植与这些严重AEs患者外周血中CD4+ T细胞亚群增加相关。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"比较对象：接受不同供体FMT的患者；治疗背景对比：黑色素瘤队列（双ICI）vs NSCLC队列及既往MIMIC试验（均为抗PD-1单药）。供体5在MIMIC试验（抗PD-1单药）中提供的7次FMT均未导致3级及以上AEs，而在本试验黑色素瘤队列中导致的FMT均伴随严重AEs。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"该研究阐明了FMT增强ICI疗效的机制并非主要依赖于供体菌株的定植或供主微生物组的相似度，而是取决于患者基线有害菌群的清除。具体来说，响应者（Responders）在接受FMT后表现出比非响应者更显著的基线细菌物种丢失（SGB loss），特别是那些已知与ICI耐药相关的有害菌属（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus等）。这种有害菌的消除导致了色氨酸代谢途径的减弱，降低了血浆中喹啉酸（quinolinic acid）和犬尿氨酸（kynurenine）的水平，从而改善了免疫代谢微环境（增加效应CD8+ T细胞，减少调节性T细胞）。关于毒性机制，研究发现特定的供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制剂（抗PD-1 + 抗CTLA-4）背景下的严重免疫相关不良事件（如心肌炎）存在情境依赖性关联。这种毒性风险在单药抗PD-1治疗中并未出现，提示供体选择需根据具体的ICI治疗方案进行优化。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制（如通过何种抗原或代谢物激活特定T细胞亚群）在本研究中仅表现为相关性，未深入解析其下游信号通路。\\\", \\\"虽然发现了基线有害菌丢失是疗效的关键预测因子，但哪些特定的丢失菌种组合对疗效贡献最大，以及是否可以通过定向清除而非全菌群移植来实现这一效果，仍需进一步研究。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是 Ch5/Ch6 核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是 Ch5/Ch6 核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R23\\\"]}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\\\", \\\"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\\\", \\\"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::163a7a8481c0223f6106b97e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"tool_supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的客观缓解率（ORR）具体数据，以及安全性特征。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在FMT-LUMINate试验中，接受健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1单药治疗的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者（n=20），其客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者（n=20），ORR为75%（15/20）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"NSCLC队列：一线治疗，无驱动基因突变，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）。黑色素瘤队列：一线或既往辅助治疗后复发>6个月，使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"揭示供体菌群特征（Prevotella富集）与特定毒性（心肌炎、3级及以上AEs）的关联机制，强调治疗背景（双免疫抑制 vs 单药）的关键调节作用。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"供体微生物组聚类显示，Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.，如Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）FMT的患者发生了严重的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），包括3例心肌炎（发生率15%），且发病时间显著提前（中位40天，而文献报道通常为60天）。其中2例心肌炎患者均接受了供体5的FMT，发病迅速（分别为第22天和第25天）。统计分析显示，Cluster B供体的粪便仅在双PD-1和CTLA-4阻断背景下导致毒性（P=0.051），而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下未观察到此类毒性。此外，S. copri的定植与这些严重AEs患者外周血中CD4+ T细胞亚群增加相关。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"比较对象：接受不同供体FMT的患者；治疗背景对比：黑色素瘤队列（双ICI）vs NSCLC队列及既往MIMIC试验（均为抗PD-1单药）。供体5在MIMIC试验（抗PD-1单药）中提供的7次FMT均未导致3级及以上AEs，而在本试验黑色素瘤队列中导致的FMT均伴随严重AEs。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"该研究阐明了FMT增强ICI疗效的机制并非主要依赖于供体菌株的定植或供主微生物组的相似度，而是取决于患者基线有害菌群的清除。具体来说，响应者（Responders）在接受FMT后表现出比非响应者更显著的基线细菌物种丢失（SGB loss），特别是那些已知与ICI耐药相关的有害菌属（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus等）。这种有害菌的消除导致了色氨酸代谢途径的减弱，降低了血浆中喹啉酸（quinolinic acid）和犬尿氨酸（kynurenine）的水平，从而改善了免疫代谢微环境（增加效应CD8+ T细胞，减少调节性T细胞）。关于毒性机制，研究发现特定的供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制剂（抗PD-1 + 抗CTLA-4）背景下的严重免疫相关不良事件（如心肌炎）存在情境依赖性关联。这种毒性风险在单药抗PD-1治疗中并未出现，提示供体选择需根据具体的ICI治疗方案进行优化。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制（如通过何种抗原或代谢物激活特定T细胞亚群）在本研究中仅表现为相关性，未深入解析其下游信号通路。\\\", \\\"虽然发现了基线有害菌丢失是疗效的关键预测因子，但哪些特定的丢失菌种组合对疗效贡献最大，以及是否可以通过定向清除而非全菌群移植来实现这一效果，仍需进一步研究。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是 Ch5/Ch6 核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是 Ch5/Ch6 核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R23\\\"]}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\\\", \\\"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\\\", \\\"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\\\", \\\"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"material_depth\": \"\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"reading_role\": \"\",\n                \"section_path\": [],\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的客观缓解率（ORR）具体数据，以及安全性特征。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在FMT-LUMINate试验中，接受健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1单药治疗的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者（n=20），其客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者（n=20），ORR为75%（15/20）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"NSCLC队列：一线治疗，无驱动基因突变，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）。黑色素瘤队列：一线或既往辅助治疗后复发>6个月，使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"揭示供体菌群特征（Prevotella富集）与特定毒性（心肌炎、3级及以上AEs）的关联机制，强调治疗背景（双免疫抑制 vs 单药）的关键调节作用。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"供体微生物组聚类显示，Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.，如Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）FMT的患者发生了严重的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），包括3例心肌炎（发生率15%），且发病时间显著提前（中位40天，而文献报道通常为60天）。其中2例心肌炎患者均接受了供体5的FMT，发病迅速（分别为第22天和第25天）。统计分析显示，Cluster B供体的粪便仅在双PD-1和CTLA-4阻断背景下导致毒性（P=0.051），而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下未观察到此类毒性。此外，S. copri的定植与这些严重AEs患者外周血中CD4+ T细胞亚群增加相关。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"比较对象：接受不同供体FMT的患者；治疗背景对比：黑色素瘤队列（双ICI）vs NSCLC队列及既往MIMIC试验（均为抗PD-1单药）。供体5在MIMIC试验（抗PD-1单药）中提供的7次FMT均未导致3级及以上AEs，而在本试验黑色素瘤队列中导致的FMT均伴随严重AEs。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"该研究阐明了FMT增强ICI疗效的机制并非主要依赖于供体菌株的定植或供主微生物组的相似度，而是取决于患者基线有害菌群的清除。具体来说，响应者（Responders）在接受FMT后表现出比非响应者更显著的基线细菌物种丢失（SGB loss），特别是那些已知与ICI耐药相关的有害菌属（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus等）。这种有害菌的消除导致了色氨酸代谢途径的减弱，降低了血浆中喹啉酸（quinolinic acid）和犬尿氨酸（kynurenine）的水平，从而改善了免疫代谢微环境（增加效应CD8+ T细胞，减少调节性T细胞）。关于毒性机制，研究发现特定的供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制剂（抗PD-1 + 抗CTLA-4）背景下的严重免疫相关不良事件（如心肌炎）存在情境依赖性关联。这种毒性风险在单药抗PD-1治疗中并未出现，提示供体选择需根据具体的ICI治疗方案进行优化。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制（如通过何种抗原或代谢物激活特定T细胞亚群）在本研究中仅表现为相关性，未深入解析其下游信号通路。\\\", \\\"虽然发现了基线有害菌丢失是疗效的关键预测因子，但哪些特定的丢失菌种组合对疗效贡献最大，以及是否可以通过定向清除而非全菌群移植来实现这一效果，仍需进一步研究。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::beb1fe084d7294818a32b847\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7617090eb1007aa68498b6fa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e3512766ef2d4d52a7760066\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a narrative review, synthesizing evidence from historical milestones, recent high-throughput sequencing studies, spatial profiling, and mechanistic in vitro/in vivo experiments. They organized the content into thematic sections: historical/methodological foundations, bacterial characterization (origin/diversity), effects on tumor initiation/progression, roles in metastasis, immune crosstalk, diagnostic/prognostic value, and therapeutic applications. The review integrates findings from various cancer types, emphasizing context-dependency and methodological rigor (e.g., distinguishing correlation from causation, addressing contamination issues).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::73b1770797f173cefdb41660\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive framework linking intratumoral bacteria to all stages of cancer progression, from initiation to metastasis and therapy response. Highlights the bidirectional nature of immune modulation and the importance of context-dependency.\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a review, it synthesizes existing literature rather than generating new primary data. Many cited mechanisms are based on specific model systems (e.g., mouse models, cell lines) or correlative human studies; causal relationships in humans require further validation. The field faces significant methodological challenges regarding low biomass and contamination that limit the robustness of some conclusions.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::008594d9c6e5593d51ba00ca\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Across multiple solid tumors, using sequencing and spatial methods\",\n          \"finding\": \"Intratumoral bacteria are prevalent, tissue-specific, and metabolically active, not merely contaminants. Their composition varies significantly by cancer type and anatomical site.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::949f2edad1df44d7aa77d089\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic studies (in vitro/vivo)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Bacteria like Fusobacterium nucleatum (Fn) and Enterotoxigenic Bacteroides fragilis (ETBF) promote tumorigenesis via genomic instability (colibactin, fragilysin), epigenetic reprogramming, and activation of oncogenic pathways (Wnt/β-catenin, PI3K/AKT).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::78c302486e7f21f1e486dcec\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Metastasis models\",\n          \"finding\": \"Intratumoral bacteria facilitate metastasis by inducing EMT, remodeling host cell cytoskeletons to resist shear stress, promoting angiogenesis, and establishing pre-metastatic niches via extracellular vesicles and vascular barrier disruption.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c51f2463bfce37ed4a4790da\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Immune modulation contexts\",\n          \"finding\": \"Effects are bidirectional and context-dependent. Pro-tumor bacteria (e.g., Fn, P. gingivalis) often induce immunosuppression (MDSC recruitment, T-cell exhaustion, PD-L1 upregulation), while beneficial taxa (e.g., Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) can enhance anti-tumor immunity and improve responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3874e95eeb3bb1557b3306e6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Clinical cohorts\",\n          \"finding\": \"Specific microbial signatures correlate with patient prognosis and survival. Intratumoral bacteria also influence response to chemotherapy (resistance or sensitization), radiotherapy, and immunotherapy, suggesting potential as biomarkers and therapeutic targets.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f33da6121926988664675bc5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c8ef3947745762d5f9e42606\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"To provide a systematic overview of the current understanding of intratumoral microbiota, addressing how these microbes originate, colonize, and functionally interact with tumor cells and the immune system to influence cancer progression and treatment outcomes, while highlighting methodological challenges and future translational directions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0f7a5addbcbd7b533b8eccb6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on intratumoral bacteria (and to a lesser extent fungi and viruses) within solid tumors. It covers their origins, colonization mechanisms, diversity across cancer types, roles in tumor initiation/progression/metastasis, interactions with the immune microenvironment, diagnostic/prognostic value, and therapeutic implications including immunotherapy response.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::21b48910c2bbb8f8ccb3bfb2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This is a comprehensive review synthesizing current knowledge on the role of intratumoral microbiota in cancer biology. It traces the historical evolution from early observations to modern multi-omics approaches, detailing methodological advances and challenges such as low biomass and contamination. The paper systematically categorizes the mechanisms by which intratumoral bacteria drive tumorigenesis (genomic instability, epigenetic changes, oncogenic signaling), promote metastasis (EMT, cytoskeletal remodeling, pre-metastatic niche formation), and modulate the immune landscape (suppression vs. activation). Furthermore, it evaluates the clinical utility of intratumoral bacteria as biomarkers for diagnosis and prognosis, and explores emerging therapeutic strategies targeting these microbes, including engineered bacteria, probiotics, antibiotics, and bacteriophages, particularly in the context of enhancing conventional therapies like chemotherapy, radiotherapy, and immunotherapy.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7f8eb404a35ab674579c1745\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of low biomass, contamination risks, and the need for rigorous controls (negative controls, spatial validation) in microbiome research.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e27e7363938b94bf5cafdb8a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Overview of engineered bacteria, probiotics, antibiotics, and bacteriophages as adjuvants to cancer therapy, including ICIs.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::54b1c990cc319087ad54b286\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Brief mention of fungal-viral-bacterial interactions in the TME.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::84a7316064bb585fd3c5eb48\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Focuses primarily on *intratumoral* bacteria, whereas the user's query specifies *gut* microbiome. However, the review notes connections between gut/oral commensals and intratumoral colonization (e.g., hematogenous spread of Fn), providing a bridge. Clinical evidence cited is largely from preclinical models or small human cohorts; large-scale prospective data specifically isolating gut vs. intra-tumor effects on ICI response is limited in this text.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Summarizes clinical associations between intratumoral microbial composition and ICI response in solid tumors (e.g., melanoma, NSCLC, CRC). Identifies specific taxa associated with better or worse outcomes (e.g., Bifidobacterium linked to improved anti-PD-L1 efficacy; Fn linked to resistance in MSS-CRC). Discusses the concept of 'microbiome-guided precision oncology' and potential for microbiome interventions to sensitize tumors to ICIs.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a808293b102fa5821c8a3af3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d36f9ec6bddaf6a75ddd347b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0535\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Mechanisms described are often derived from animal models or in vitro studies. The review acknowledges that many associations are correlative and causal validation in humans is ongoing. The distinction between direct bacterial effects and indirect effects mediated by other gut-derived factors is sometimes blurred in the synthesis.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details specific molecular mechanisms by whi